# ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Repo-root build context (Dockerfile.service, Dockerfile.nextjs,
# Dockerfile.db-migrate). Keeps secrets, local artifacts and the dependency
# tree out of images and build cache.
#
# CRITICAL: `.env` is secrets — never bake it. `node_modules` would overwrite
# the fresh `npm ci` install inside the builder with this machine's binaries.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
**/dist
**/build

.git
.github
.vscode
.idea

# Local run artifacts (boot logs, PIDs, probes, APKs)
.setuprun
*.log
*.apk

# Per-engine stray binaries (bulk-processor.exe etc.)
**/*.exe
**/__pycache__

# Docs and CI don't belong in images
docs
*.md
!turbo.json

# Mobile apps build outside Docker — but their package.json must stay in the
# context (they are npm workspaces; npm ci resolves the full lockfile).
apps/mobile_flutter/android
apps/mobile_flutter/ios
apps/mobile_flutter/.expo
apps/mobile_flutter/.dart_tool
apps/mobile/android
apps/mobile/ios

# Docker files themselves aren't needed inside images
docker
